# {{ .Project.Name }}

Run `go test ./...`, `go build ./...`, and `go run ./cmd/service`.
Export the variables in .env.example to override typed local defaults.
Dotenv files are not loaded automatically. /healthz returns 204.

The service has no database, authentication, or business logic.
Entity scaffolds use parent types plus controller, service, and repository
packages, wired through explicit constructors in cmd/service.
Repository placeholders return ErrNotImplemented and handlers return HTTP 501.

{{ if .Settings.workflow }}
Temporal SDK v1.29.1 is included. The registry is empty: startup does not
connect, poll, or execute workflows. Explicit registrations activate the
adapter. TEMPORAL_DIAL_TIMEOUT bounds the complete startup wait, including
namespace lookup. Startup RPCs receive that deadline and cancellation. One
owner serializes SDK Start, SDK Stop, and client close, including late completion.
Temporal cleanup waits with a fresh APP_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT context after a
signal or failure, separate from HTTP shutdown and its own timeout.
That budget bounds the caller's wait; if it expires, the owner continues cleanup.
TEMPORAL_WORKER_STOP_TIMEOUT is an SDK timeout per worker component. SDK v1.29.1
stops local activity, workflow, and activity components sequentially, so the
5s default can take 15s or more overall. It is not a total shutdown deadline.
SDK Stop has no context argument; the client closes after SDK Stop completes.
{{ else }}
Temporal is disabled; the Go source uses only the standard library.
{{ end }}
